        <p style="color:rgba(220,215,201,0.85);">Shimul Rajput is a Registered Psychotherapist (Qualifying) with a Master of Arts in Counselling Psychology (MACP) from Yorkville University, and dual BSc degrees in Psychology and Health Studies from the University of Toronto.</p>
        <p style="color:rgba(220,215,201,0.85);">With over four years of clinical experience, Shimul integrates evidence-based therapies — including CBT, DBT, mindfulness, EFCT, and narrative approaches — to compassionately support individuals and couples navigating anxiety, self-worth, identity, and relationship challenges.</p>
        <p style="color:rgba(220,215,201,0.85);">As a South Asian therapist, Shimul is deeply dedicated to decolonizing the therapy space and uplifting BIPOC voices. Her practice is grounded in empathy, authenticity, and the conviction that true healing unfolds within safe, collaborative spaces.</p>
